      <h2>What makes a Home Counties move different</h2>
      <p>The Home Counties cover a wide mix of village, market-town and commuter-belt properties, often with access considerations a city move simply doesn&rsquo;t have &mdash; long driveways, narrow lanes, or limited parking near the property on moving day. We plan the logistics of your move around these details from the first call, not on the morning itself.</p>
      <p>Many of the moves we support here involve clients relocating between villages, or from a larger rural property into something more manageable nearby &mdash; often while staying close to a community, GP surgery or family network they don&rsquo;t want to leave behind. That local continuity is usually as important as the move itself.</p>
      <p>A number of these moves also involve selling a larger family home to release equity for a smaller, more manageable one nearby, which means the sale side needs coordinating alongside the physical move rather than treated as a separate job for a separate company. Where that's the case, staging and estate agent liaison run in parallel with the sorting and packing, so neither holds the other up.</p>
      <div class="area-honest">
        <p>We&rsquo;re based in Northampton, which sits within practical reach of much of the Home Counties &mdash; keeping response times realistic for both viewings and moving day. We work with clients across the UK, and the Home Counties are among the areas we support most often given our location.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
